<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=1080, initial-scale=1">
<title>Specimen — Ep.2 end card A/B (Action #35)</title>
<!--
  SPECIMEN SCENE for Action #35 (req-engagement-overlays) — JOB B29, 2026-10-25.
  NOT a production scene: a board specimen carrying the two 3.0 s Ep.2
  end-card loops (A spoken-only / B one silent bell) side by side so the
  ask is decidable from the board at phone size. Loops embedded
  byte-for-byte; sources + md5s in the decisions block below.
-->
<style>
  @font-face { font-family: "Patrick Hand"; src: url(data:font/ttf;base64,) format("truetype"); }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  html, body { width: 1080px; height: 1920px; overflow: hidden; background: #171208;
               font-family: "Patrick Hand", cursive; color: #f5efe0; }
  .wrap { padding: 84px 48px 0 48px; }
  h1 { font-size: 74px; line-height: 1.12; text-align: center; font-weight: normal; }
  h1 .amber { color: #ffb040; }
  .sub { margin-top: 30px; font-size: 44px; line-height: 1.25; text-align: center; color: #d8cfb8; }
  .cols { display: flex; gap: 24px; margin-top: 64px; }
  .col { width: 480px; }
  .lab { font-size: 46px; text-align: center; color: #ffb040; margin-bottom: 22px;
         height: 118px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; justify-content: center; }
  .col video { width: 480px; height: 854px; object-fit: cover; display: block;
               border-radius: 18px; background: #000; }
  .cap { margin-top: 22px; font-size: 39px; line-height: 1.28; text-align: center; color: #efe8d5; }
  .foot { margin-top: 58px; font-size: 46px; text-align: center; color: #d8cfb8; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">
  <h1>Ep.2&rsquo;s end card &mdash;<br>the same three seconds, <span class="amber">two ways</span></h1>
  <div class="sub">Both loops play. On the right card, watch the right side<br>at 2 seconds &mdash; that is the whole question.</div>
  <div class="cols">
    <div class="col">
      <div class="lab">A &mdash; SPOKEN-ONLY, AS BUILT</div>
      <video src="data:video/mp4;base64," autoplay muted loop playsinline></video>
      <div class="cap">The ask rides the spoken line<br>and the card text. Nothing else appears.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="col">
      <div class="lab">B &mdash; ONE SILENT BELL</div>
      <video src="data:video/mp4;base64," autoplay muted loop playsinline></video>
      <div class="cap">A small cream bell fades in 2 s<br>into the card, clear of every line of text.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="foot">Same card, same seconds &mdash; the bell is the only difference.</div>
</div>
<script type="application/json" id="decisions">{
 "coverage": "2 of 2 elements recorded · 0 undecided (specimen scene, JOB B29)",
 "records": [
  {
   "id": "DR-SPEC-1",
   "element": "Specimen fidelity — the two end-card loops",
   "choice": "The specimen embeds the two original 3.0 s end-card loops byte-for-byte (A: ep2-endcard-nobell-loop.mp4, md5 af7421d9d5fb74b12b1a84a2f8db79f2; B: ep2-endcard-bell-loop.mp4, md5 e8cf4ed060593a9f316ea070ae8adba2; both 540x960, from hidden_files/context-coverage-2026-10-23/media/). No re-encode, no trim: what Hadi sees is the exact segment the ask was written on.",
   "alternatives": "Rebuilding the B card inside the Ep.2 v4 production scene — rejected: it would pre-decide Action #35 inside a production artifact. Linking the local files — rejected: local references do not play on the served board (the board's media rule).",
   "context": "Action #35 (req-engagement-overlays) failed badge item (f) in JOB BADGE-GATE: option B's bell existed only as a local file named in prose; the board compare plays the Ep.2 v3/v2 scenes, neither of which contains the bell. JOB B29 gives the ask a specimen scene of its own.",
   "why": "A visual choice must be decidable from the ask itself, at phone size, in under five minutes — the specimen is the two cards, side by side, looping.",
   "change": "Action #35's verdict closes the question this specimen serves; the scene then stands as the A/B record."
  },
  {
   "id": "DR-SPEC-2",
   "element": "Specimen layout + behaviour",
   "choice": "1080x1920 stage: a title line, the two loops side by side at native 540x960 (A left, B right), a label over each and one caption line under each, one closing line. Both videos autoplay, muted, looping, inline — a specimen of three seconds has nothing to scrub; the board's tap-to-play overlay is deliberately not engaged (the scene carries no audio element and no #stage/#playbtn hooks, so the board's scene-state probe leaves it alone). A tap anywhere toggles both loops together.",
   "alternatives": "Stacked full-width loops (each 1080 wide, cropped) — rejected: cropping the card would hide the bell's position against the text, which is the decision. A toggle showing one card at a time — rejected: the board's A/B grammar is side-by-side (the compare), and the difference must be visible in one glance.",
   "context": "Board compare grammar (showCompare: two cells, each playing its own copy); the bell sits at x 812-948, y 1132-1268 of the 1080-wide master frame — in this layout's B cell it lands in the cell's lower right, clear of the card text.",
   "why": "Side-by-side at native size is the fastest honest read of a one-glyph difference.",
   "change": "If the phone-size eyeball (JOB B29) finds the bell unreadable at this size, the layout — not the loops — is reworked."
  }
 ]
}</script>
<script>
  const vids = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll("video"));
  vids.forEach(v => { const p = v.play(); if (p) p.catch(() => {}); });
  document.addEventListener("click", () => {
    const anyPaused = vids.some(v => v.paused);
    vids.forEach(v => { if (anyPaused) v.play(); else v.pause(); });
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
